{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement, `y ~ poisson_log(...)`, after both parameters have received their built-in priors. Other data variables are used only as context inputs.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> M; // Number of covariates
  int<lower=0> N; // Number of observations

  vector[M] x0;   // Covariate baselines
  matrix[N, M] X; // Covariate design matrix

  array[N] int y;       // Variates
}

transformed data {
  matrix[N, M] deltaX;
  for (n in 1:N) {
    deltaX[n,] = X[n] - x0';
  }
}

parameters {
  real alpha;          // Intercept
  vector[M] beta;      // Slopes
}

model {
  // Prior model
  alpha ~ normal(3, 0.2);
  beta ~ normal(0, log(1.28));

  // Vectorized observation model
  y ~ poisson_log(alpha + deltaX * beta);
}

// Simulate a full observation from the current value of the parameters
generated quantities {
  vector[N] mu = exp(alpha + deltaX * beta);
  array[N] int y_pred = poisson_log_rng(alpha + deltaX * beta);
}
